    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="990O" softwareId="24019898" softwareVersionNum="24.0.1.0">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 4B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>LITERACY Build A Miracle continues to receive more and more primary and middle school age children unable to attend public school because they are too many years below grade level, many unable to read or write. In 2023 BAM purposefully added remedial classes and began working on a strategy to advance them to grade level before they completely lose the opportunity to receive a formal education. TRADES BUSINESSES in 2024 BAM supported the startup or growth of 45 small businesses and offered training and other support to an additional 104. 68 individuals/families sold BAM Bakery sweet bread in their communities, bringing in income for their families. Hair Cosmetology programs increased in size and scope with 389 participants and the addition of Master Classes given by teachers from around the world.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 2</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CHRISTOPHER NORTH AND JULIANNE NORTH HAVE A FAMILY RELATIONSHIP. BUDDY THOMAS AND ELIZABETH THOMAS HAVE A FAMILY RELATIONSHIP.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section A, Line 8B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>BUILD A MIRACLE IS A SMALL ORGANIZATION THAT OPERATES WITHOUT SUBCOMMITTEEES. IF A SUBCOMMITTEE WERE TO BE REQUIRED IN THE FUTURE, IT WOULD BE FORMED AND APPOPRIATE WRITTEN DOCUMENTATION KEPT.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE PRESIDENT REVIEWS THE FORM 990 WITH OTHER BOARD MEMBERS AND OUTSIDE SUPPORTAND AND ANY NECESSARY ADJUSTMENTS ARE MADE BEFORE FINALIZING AND FILING THE RETURN. THE OTHER MEMBERS OF THE BOARD ARE ALSO PROVIDED A COPY OF THE FILING AND INPUT IS SOLICITED AND INCORPORATED AS RELEVANT.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>ALL OFFICERS AND DIRECTORS ARE REQUIRED TO COMPLETE AN ANNUAL CONFLICT OF INTEREST DISCLOSURE FORM. ALL OFFICERS AND DIRECTORS ARE ALSO REQUIRED TO PROMPTLY AND FULLY DISCLOSE ALL POTENTIAL CONFLICTS OF INTEREST. ANY PERSON WITH A CONFLICT WITH RESPECT TO ANY MATTER MUST EXCUSE HIM/HERSELF FROM ANY DISCUSSION OR VOTE WITH RESPECT TO SUCH MATTER. THERE HAVE BEEN NO INCIDENCES OF CONFLICT DURING THE REPORTING YEAR</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>COMPENSATED IS DETERMINED BY BOARD OF DIRECTORS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAKES AVAILABLE ITS GOVERNING DOCUMENTS AS REQUESTED.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part XII, Line 2C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION ENGAGES AN INDEPENDENT AUDITING FIRM TO CONDUCT AUDITS AS REQUIRED BY THE BOARD. THE PRESIDENT OF THE BOARD OVERSEES THE AUDIT PROCESS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part XI, Line 9</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Donated salaries of 80,000 and donated rent of 20,000 were excluded per IRS regulations.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part IX, Line 11g</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The Organization pays stipends to community members, mostly women from the homes we build, to support the efforts of the team to find new families, encourage participation in all of our programs, build community, etc.</ExplanationTxt>
